- No. No. Not you.


01:39:56.530 --> 01:39:58.315
Here. Drink some water. Come on.


01:39:58.489 --> 01:40:00.230
What's happening? You can't breathe?


01:40:00.404 --> 01:40:01.579
Drink some water. Come on.


01:40:06.018 --> 01:40:07.585
What is it? Are you having
a panic attack right now?


01:40:09.892 --> 01:40:11.807
You need to breathe. You're not
breathing properly. Come here.


01:40:15.114 --> 01:40:16.507
Hey, hey, it's all right.


01:40:22.165 --> 01:40:25.777
Hey, hey, hey. Hey. No, no, no.


01:40:33.698 --> 01:40:34.830
I'm really sorry.


01:40:40.357 --> 01:40:41.271
Okay, I'm really sorry.


01:40:59.680 --> 01:41:01.726
It is such a huge honor


01:41:01.900 --> 01:41:04.729
to have been guided by
a woman like Romy Mathis.


01:41:05.948 --> 01:41:09.690
She understands the importance
of being a voice for your peers


01:41:09.995 --> 01:41:12.041
and an advocate for
women around the world


01:41:12.215 --> 01:41:16.567
who might not have the same
opportunities that us, sitting here, have.


01:41:16.959 --> 01:41:21.311
So to be lifted up by a hero like her


01:41:21.485 --> 01:41:23.879
makes this experience
so much more exceptional.


01:41:26.316 --> 01:41:29.188
Who are we, as women?


01:41:29.885 --> 01:41:32.931
Modern leaders aren't
afraid to take chances


01:41:33.105 --> 01:41:36.500
embrace change, and usher
a team into the unknown.


01:41:36.935 --> 01:41:40.808
Sincerity, vulnerability,
and radical self-honesty


01:41:40.983 --> 01:41:44.421
will create a work environment
of shared learning, compassion,


01:41:44.595 --> 01:41:46.466
and true connection.


01:41:46.640 --> 01:41:48.642
Now, how do we do that?


01:41:49.078 --> 01:41:51.950
By making changes from top
to bottom to support women


01:41:52.124 --> 01:41:54.474
at every level across the company.


01:41:56.389 --> 01:41:58.435
If we dare to let go of expectations


01:41:58.609 --> 01:42:01.090
and move towards what scares us,


01:42:01.264 --> 01:42:03.396
we can often find unexpected strengths.


01:42:04.180 --> 01:42:07.357
Today, we celebrate genuine authenticity


01:42:07.531 --> 01:42:11.056
and true uniqueness in every
individual that works at Tensile.


01:42:11.927 --> 01:42:15.800
We invite each other to show
the world who we really are


01:42:15.974 --> 01:42:19.630
regardless of people's
assumptions and without fear.


01:42:44.524 --> 01:42:46.222
Oh, hey.


01:42:48.137 --> 01:42:49.225
You okay?


01:42:51.401 --> 01:42:52.924
You look like Grandma.


01:42:57.450 --> 01:42:58.756
How did you get here?


01:43:00.018 --> 01:43:01.106
I got a car.


01:43:01.759 --> 01:43:02.803
You did?


01:43:03.761 --> 01:43:05.284
That's expensive.


01:43:07.156 --> 01:43:08.244
Mom...


01:43:09.506 --> 01:43:11.073
...you have to come home.


01:43:13.118 --> 01:43:14.424
Dad needs you.


01:43:17.253 --> 01:43:19.298
He won't leave the theatre.


01:43:20.256 --> 01:43:23.476
He won't eat, and
he's reading the Bible.


01:43:25.565 --> 01:43:27.393
He'll forgive you, Mom.


01:43:27.567 --> 01:43:28.829
What did he tell you?


01:43:29.830 --> 01:43:30.831
Nothing.


01:43:33.051 --> 01:43:34.661
Mary forgave me.


01:43:42.234 --> 01:43:43.844
It's okay, Mom.


01:43:46.891 --> 01:43:48.110
It's okay.


01:43:52.114 --> 01:43:52.984
God.


01:43:54.116 --> 01:43:55.247
Okay.


01:44:02.646 --> 01:44:04.082
Please come home.


01:44:29.629 --> 01:44:30.978
It's all my fault.


01:44:32.850 --> 01:44:36.071
I told you that I was
someone else and I got angry


01:44:36.245 --> 01:44:38.638
because you didn't
know who I really was.


01:44:39.161 --> 01:44:43.730
And I'm so sorry. It's my
problem. It's my problem.


01:44:44.905 --> 01:44:49.171
Hey. What a great way
to start the year, huh?


01:44:51.825 --> 01:44:53.088
Um...


01:44:55.351 --> 01:44:56.961
Whatever happened to that intern?


01:44:57.135 --> 01:44:59.746
The one who bought me the coffee?


01:45:00.312 --> 01:45:03.402
I heard he took a job
at Kawasaki? In Tokyo?


01:45:07.232 --> 01:45:08.538
Good for him.


01:45:08.712 --> 01:45:09.887
Good for you, too.


01:45:12.498 --> 01:45:14.892
You didn't have anything
to do with that, did you?


01:45:17.286 --> 01:45:19.505
Why don't you come over
next week for drinks?


01:45:19.679 --> 01:45:21.594
I've got the house to myself.


01:45:22.813 --> 01:45:24.119
We can talk about it.


01:45:30.342 --> 01:45:32.257
Why don't you fuck off, Sebastian?


01:45:32.431 --> 01:45:34.564
Hey, careful, Romy.


01:45:34.738 --> 01:45:38.742
I'm not afraid of you, whatever
the fuck you're capable of.


01:45:38.916 --> 01:45:41.788
Of what you know, of what you
don't know. I don't give a shit.


01:45:42.267 --> 01:45:46.053
Just don't ever talk
to me like that again.


01:45:46.750 --> 01:45:50.188
If I want to be humiliated,
I'm gonna pay someone to do it.


01:45:53.409 --> 01:45:55.367
Now get the fuck out of my office.


01:46:07.379 --> 01:46:08.380
Five...


01:46:10.556 --> 01:46:11.470
four...


01:46:13.733 --> 01:46:14.952
three...


01:46:16.910 --> 01:46:17.998
two...


01:46:20.131 --> 01:46:21.176
one...

